Negative control for the killed track chips (`R7-10`).

Puts the first two scenarios back on the bar as their own capped, truncating
chips — the menu is untouched, every scenario is still reachable inside it, and
Live still reads live — so the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: the
bar carries Live and ONE menu, and a scenario's name is never rendered as a
fragment beside them. A chip capped at `max-w-40` shows "A client sees their …",
which is the illegible bar the operator screenshotted.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the scenario-bar entry case — the bar draws exactly one `track` entry, and
it is Live.

